prm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">ears</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">frozen corn on the cob</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">frozen and ready to cook</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">enough</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">to cover</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Water</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for boiling</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Butter</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for serving</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for seasoning</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-7088-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7088\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Large pot&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For boiling the corn</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Colander&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For draining the corn</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-7088-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-7088-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7088\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7088-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Bring Water to a Boil &#8211; Start by bringing a large pot of water to a rolling boil. Don’t forget to add a pinch of salt to enhance the flavor!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7088-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Add the Corn &#8211; Once the water is boiling, carefully add the frozen corn on the cob to the pot. Watch out for splashes!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7088-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Boil the Corn &#8211; Let the corn boil for 5–7 minutes. You want it to be tender and heated through. The aroma will be delightful!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7088-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Drain the Corn &#8211; Carefully remove the corn from the water and drain it well. Be cautious, it’s hot!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7088-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Add Butter and Season &#8211; Brush each ear of corn with butter and sprinkle with black pepper. Yum!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7088-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Serve and Enjoy! &#8211; Serve the corn immediately while it’s hot. Enjoy your delicious frozen corn on the cob!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-7088-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>90</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>4g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>3g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>12g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s what you&#8217;ll need to prepare delicious frozen <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_corn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">corn </a>on the cob!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Frozen-Corn-on-the-Cob.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for frozen corn on the cob displayed on a rustic kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-7086\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Frozen-Corn-on-the-Cob.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Frozen-Corn-on-the-Cob-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>4 ears frozen corn on the cob</strong> – frozen and ready to cook</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Water</strong> – enough to cover corn</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Butter</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Black pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-frozen-corn-on-the-cob\"><strong>How to Make frozen corn on the cob</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making frozen corn on the cob is quick and easy! With a preparation time of just 5 minutes and a cooking time of 5–7 minutes, you can enjoy this delicious side dish in no time. Serve it hot for the best experience!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparing-Frozen-Corn-on-the-Cob.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of preparing frozen corn on the cob, from boiling to serving.\" class=\"wp-image-7087\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparing-Frozen-Corn-on-the-Cob.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparing-Frozen-Corn-on-the-Cob-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Bring Water to a Boil</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Start by bringing a large pot of water to a rolling boil. Don’t forget to add a pinch of salt to enhance the flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Add the Corn</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once the water is boiling, carefully add the frozen corn on the cob to the pot. Watch out for splashes!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Boil the Corn</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Let the corn boil for 5–7 minutes. You want it to be tender and heated through. The aroma will be delightful!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Drain the Corn</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Carefully remove the corn from the water and drain it well. Be cautious, it’s hot!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Add Butter and Season</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Brush each ear of corn with butter and sprinkle with black pepper. Yum!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Serve and Enjoy!</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve the corn immediately while it’s hot. Enjoy your delicious frozen corn on the cob!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Side Dish / Snack</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>7 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>12 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot with butter and seasoning!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-frozen-corn-on-the-cob\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making frozen corn on the cob</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw corn on the cob in the fridge overnight for best texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Brush with olive oil or melted butter for added flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Season with salt and pepper before grilling or boiling.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in foil with herbs for a delicious steam effect.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with lime wedges for a zesty finish.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-frozen-corn-on-the-cob\"><strong>How to Serve this frozen corn on the cob</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Slather with butter and sprinkle with sea salt for a classic treat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with grated Parmesan and a squeeze of lemon for a zesty twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle with honey and a dash of chili powder for a sweet and spicy kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside grilled chicken or veggie burgers for a colorful plate.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a fresh salad for a light and refreshing meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in foil with herbs and garlic for a flavorful steam in the oven.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chop and mix into a corn salad with tomatoes and avocado for a summer vibe.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to store and enjoy your frozen corn on the cob:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow corn to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container or freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and store in the fridge for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Blanch corn for 4-5 minutes in boiling water.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cool in ice water to stop cooking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drain and dry thoroughly.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap tightly in plastic wrap or foil, then place in a freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label and freeze for up to 12 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For best results, steam corn for 5-7 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Microwave with a damp paper towel for 2-3 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Grill for a smoky flavor, about 10 minutes on medium heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Check for warmth and enjoy!</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Should you defrost frozen corn on the cob before cooking?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>No, you don’t need to defrost frozen corn on the cob before cooking. In fact, cooking it straight from the freezer can help retain its flavor and texture. Just add a few extra minutes to your cooking time to ensure it heats through completely.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Is frozen corn on cob good?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Frozen corn on the cob is a convenient and tasty option. It’s picked at peak ripeness and quickly frozen to lock in flavor and nutrients, making it a great addition to your meals any time of the year.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What&#8217;s the best way to heat up frozen corn on the cob?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best way to heat up frozen corn on the cob is by boiling or grilling. For boiling, simply place the corn in a pot of boiling water for about 5-7 minutes. If you prefer grilling, wrap the corn in foil and grill for about 15-20 minutes, turning occasionally for even cooking.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How many minutes should I boil frozen corn?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>You should boil frozen corn on the cob for about 5-7 minutes. This will ensure that it’s heated through and tender without losing its delicious crunch. Just make sure to keep an eye on it to avoid overcooking!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So there you have it! Enjoying frozen corn on the cob is as easy as it gets. Picture those sunny summer days with a delicious ear of corn in hand, bursting with flavor. It’s simple, satisfying, and oh-so-rewarding. Dive in, savor every bite, and let the nostalgia of summer fill your kitchen!</p>\n",
